<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Hungarian tribal federation</h1><p class="st-meta">830 CE – 895 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Confederation of seven Magyar tribes in the steppe of Etelköz, under Khazar overlordship, that set off to conquer the Carpathian basin in 895.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Hungarians</a>, Finno-Ugric speakers who had absorbed steppe Turkic culture, moved west and by about 830 lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etelkoz">Etelköz</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a> describes seven tribes led first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levedi">Levedi</a>, under the authority of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were mounted pastoralists and fearsome raiders, selling captives to traders on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. Leadership was dual, with a sacral kende and a military gyula. Three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabars">Kabar</a> tribes, rebels from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>, joined them. They raided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/east-francia">East Francia</a> from 862 and fought for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 894. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almos">Álmos</a> and then his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a> were elected as leaders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 895 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etelkoz">Etelköz</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Hungarians</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> into the basin, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-hungary">Principality of Hungary</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 830 CE – 895 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:76.22%;width:1.29%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>830 CE – 895 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Levedi, Álmos, Árpád</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Etelköz Hungarians, Magyar confederation, Seven Magyar tribes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=862&amp;focus=hungarian-tribal-federation" aria-label="Hungarian tribal federation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5428 440 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hungarian tribal federation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5437 760h0M6131 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5748 696h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5748 696h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ukraine. <a href="/atlas?year=862&amp;focus=hungarian-tribal-federation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
